insert into public.lessons (id, kind, number, title, video_url, body, retired) values ('66bec75a-69ba-50b9-bd67-ddfe7c39c2c5', 'sbw', 9, 'Why and How to have ''Non-Negotiables'' in your life', 'https://youtu.be/-Yo0h6qG648', 'You are what you do every day

And even if you''ve been out of shape for a while... deep down, you know what needs to be done

I mean, everybody does

Not stuffing yourself. Not starving either.

Moving every day.

Drinking water.

Showing love. And having a positive attitude.

Simple stuff. And easy to do.

But what''s easy to do, is also easy not to do.

And I think it''s when we take these essential actions for granted that we spiral downward so negatively - until we end up desperate for change, and this is where ''quick fixes'' and fads become appealing.

Wherever you are on this spiral, you can change starting today. Simply focus on 1 action every day, in 4 areas of your life.

Every day, have ''non-negotiables'' that you do every single day.

These are things you will absolutely, positively get done - no matter WHAT.

Check this video to see what area of your life to have non-negotiables in.

Simple stuff, but it works

Because you are... what you do every day.', false) on conflict (id) do update set title = excluded.title, video_url = coalesce(public.lessons.video_url, excluded.video_url), body = coalesce(public.lessons.body, excluded.body), retired = excluded.retired;
insert into public.lessons (id, kind, number, title, video_url, body, retired) values ('220306fd-3da0-5af3-81b8-91e909cedb2b', 'sbw', 10, 'Why most people quit too soon', 'https://youtu.be/VAG1VdTYDMA', 'I often post Before/Afters and share clients of mine who have completely transformed their life by getting in shape and making it a lifestyle

But...

Not all my clients actually get results

Some of them pay a bunch of money, and get nothing in return

I mean, they get my coaching. And I''m there for them, helping them to the best of my ability.

But if a client is not mentally ready to change, then no external help will ever make an impact

See any time you want to change something in your life, you will go through the ''emotional cycle of change''

First you start

And you''re motivated

You don''t know what to expect, but you''re optimistic

Then you find out it takes a lot of hard work

And your initial motivation and optimism fades

This, is called ''the valley of despair''

Every person, every program, every single instance has this ''valley of despair''

Because everything worthwhile takes effort

And it''s when you go through this valley of despair that you''re at your most vulnerable of quitting

And when you quit, you start something else

... only to end up in the same valley of despair, and the cycle repeats

I made you a video on this, showing you exactly what this looks like in a graph

In my video you''ll also see how to ''arm'' yourself for this and not let the valley of despair stop you from getting the success you ultimately want', false) on conflict (id) do update set title = excluded.title, video_url = coalesce(public.lessons.video_url, excluded.video_url), body = coalesce(public.lessons.body, excluded.body), retired = excluded.retired;
