insert into public.lessons (id, kind, number, title, video_url, body, retired) values ('4e3fa764-cca7-5a87-bbe5-1cef8ad327c5', 'sbw', 38, 'Something you need to know about Meal #1', 'https://youtu.be/SGgS98NL-3M', 'Lately I''ve been telling everyone who wants to hear it that my acai bowl is the greatest acai bowl in the world

And I mean it. Most acai bowls are all sugar, no protein.

Mine is real fruit only, and loaded with hundreds of bald eagle proteins that fly straight into your muscle.

Mine also has magnesium and all kinds of nutrients from the superfoods I add

It''s truly a work of art. I''d rather eat my acai bowl than go see the tower of Pisa.

But a couple weeks ago, I discovered something interesting

See I''ve been doing Intermittent Fasting for a while now

Wake up at 5:30am. Start eating around 11am.

Usually my acai bowl is meal #1 (what I ''break'' my fast with).

But a couple weeks ago I decided to switch it up.

I had my bison & potatoes as meal #1, and my acai bowl later on at night.

And as I was sitting on my couch, consuming my acai bowl while watching Millionaire Matchmaker

(j/k I was watching Better Call Saul)

... I realized that my acai bowl wasn''t as ''tasty'' as usual

I said ''huh'' out loud (I said that out loud)

And thought maybe I put in the wrong amount of ingredients or something

But when I tried this again a couple days later - same thing happened

My acai bowl seemed to taste different at night

Then I got to thinking...

And I discovered something truly groundbreaking when it comes to your first meal of the day

So...

I made you a video on it =)

And since I know you''re busy, I incorporated Mariah Carey and the Little Mermaid in order to explain what I mean', false) on conflict (id) do update set title = excluded.title, video_url = coalesce(public.lessons.video_url, excluded.video_url), body = coalesce(public.lessons.body, excluded.body), retired = excluded.retired;
insert into public.lessons (id, kind, number, title, video_url, body, retired) values ('08872ee8-7ddb-52cf-b60c-95e194c8b5aa', 'sbw', 39, 'Why are we doing Intermittent Fasting again?', 'https://youtu.be/JT87jS3PGAw', 'The #1 benefit of Intermittent Fasting is that it''s a creative way to ''cut calories''

Or more, cut the ''time'' you have available to you to get calories in

If you only have 8 hours you can eat every day, versus 16 - you already know it''s going to be harder to overshoot on calories if you have less time to eat

But there are many more benefits to Intermittent Fasting then just that

And with new diets and tricks coming out every day, I wanted to make you this quick reminder on all the reasons I recommend IF if you want to get lean, stay lean, and do it the ''easy way''.', true) on conflict (id) do update set title = excluded.title, video_url = coalesce(public.lessons.video_url, excluded.video_url), body = coalesce(public.lessons.body, excluded.body), retired = excluded.retired;
insert into public.lessons (id, kind, number, title, video_url, body, retired) values ('1dea3404-ddd3-58f3-954d-6006ad157161', 'sbw', 40, 'Reminder on why Almonds are a must', 'https://youtu.be/zO07ovgPQPA', 'You already know almonds are practically magical

Every single fitness magazine, every online fitness influencer

PROBABLY even your mother-in-law knows about almonds

They are healthy

But as with everything holy and pure, sometimes big companies get it twisted (like Keith Sweat)

And they mess it all up

So I made you a quick video on ''what kind'' of almond to get (and the difference between sprouted vs non-sprouted)

Click here to see it: {Training Magic Link training_slug=strong-body-wednesday-40}', false) on conflict (id) do update set title = excluded.title, video_url = coalesce(public.lessons.video_url, excluded.video_url), body = coalesce(public.lessons.body, excluded.body), retired = excluded.retired;
insert into public.lessons (id, kind, number, title, video_url, body, retired) values ('3fd0d3c3-46cc-58ac-a5ba-09b78956eed8', 'sbw', 41, 'Never eat standing up', 'https://youtu.be/bWkzVQouzCQ', 'Your subconscious mind will ''adapt'' to how you eat

What I mean is...

If you eat standing up, scarfing your food down as fast as possible - your body and mind will ''assume'' that food is not really a priority for you

And you will continue to act in accordance with that belief

"Food is not important enough to sit down for, therefore the types of foods I eat don''t matter anyway"

Imagine on the other hand... making every meal awesome

Sitting DOWN for every meal...

You would put more effort into what goes into that meal

And...

An added benefit to sitting down for each meal will have you chew your food more thoroughly.

Which in turn improves digestion and nutrient absorption.

Click here to see a video on what I mean, and to claim some XP points by answering a question on how often you should chew your food: {Training Magic Link training_slug=strong-body-wednesday-41}', false) on conflict (id) do update set title = excluded.title, video_url = coalesce(public.lessons.video_url, excluded.video_url), body = coalesce(public.lessons.body, excluded.body), retired = excluded.retired;
insert into public.lessons (id, kind, number, title, video_url, body, retired) values ('496a7f4c-763c-5d96-b371-031462c86571', 'sbw', 42, 'How to Replace your bad addictions', 'https://youtu.be/TF_wgorscfs', 'My Mom was born in Amsterdam in 1947

2 years after the war. Then she went to the USA as an au pair in the 70''s.

That was quite the adventure back then. She would mail cassette tapes back home to let everyone know how she was doing.

In 1983 I was born, in La Crescenta, CA

I was born into the American lifestyle

And at the age of 8, my Mom decided to move back to Holland - primarily because she thought it would be better for my upbringing

I think she was right too.

Because had I stayed in USA, I probably would''ve turned obese

Or at least very, very fat

I loved twinkies, Oreos, I was not eating healthy as a kid here. And all I did was stay home and play videogames.

Then I remember my first day being in Holland, all the local kids in the village heard there was an American in town

So they rang the doorbell, and asked if I wanted to come play soccer with them

That was a rude awakening in which I discovered how out of shape I was

And from that day on, literally every single day we''d play soccer outside after school
(and if the rain was too much, we''d play FIFA at someone''s house till we could go out again)

Rain, shine, or even with ice on the field - we would play soccer if our parents let us

All the way till 5pm. Because that''s when you would hear Moms yell out ''Etenstijd'' (which means ''dinnertime'')

As I grew up there, I forged an iron discipline

If we ran out of milk, I had to bicycle to the grocery store and get some

Rain or shine

When I started going to college, I had to catch the 5:50am train to Amsterdam

Which meant I had to bicycle at 5:20am to the train station

Rain or shine

Then when I''d get back home from a day at school, I would bicycle to the gym, which was another 45 minutes the opposite direction

Discipline was all I knew

So when I moved to America at age 23, I was set to make things happen

I would do whatever it took to get what I wanted. Because, in case you need to hear this again, California is paradise compared to almost everywhere else in the world.

That discipline led me to push forward, and eventually build a business where I had 3 gyms serving over 1,000 clients every month

Reason I''m saying this is because this discipline and ''zest'' for life served me well

Then, back in 2017 or 2018, I started training the 4am sessions at my gym.

And I wanted a way to fall asleep easier

So, long story short, I started dabbling into THC

And what started with an innocent means to get better sleep, turned into total disrupt into my discipline and daily habits

I made a video on what happened exactly, and how I got myself out of this just last year

And I''m sharing it with you because I have a feeling I''m not the only one that has struggled with bad ''addictions''

I got rid of mine, but only after I replaced the voids they left.', false) on conflict (id) do update set title = excluded.title, video_url = coalesce(public.lessons.video_url, excluded.video_url), body = coalesce(public.lessons.body, excluded.body), retired = excluded.retired;
insert into public.lessons (id, kind, number, title, video_url, body, retired) values ('304041b3-045a-5fb4-bdb1-f3789bf66b1e', 'sbw', 43, 'How much caffeine should you have every day?', 'https://youtu.be/P8JVCcR25XE', 'Caffeine is kind of a weird subject

It has massive benefits (kills hunger, provides energy, warms up your joints pre-workouts)

But it can also mess with your sleep, stress, hormones, and mood

So I personally don''t take more than 200 mg per day

But, I also have clients born in El Salvador who have been drinking coffee since they were little kids (and their parents still live there happily and healthy at age 90+)

So is caffeine evil?

Claro que no

But I do think in our high-paced American lifestyle - it''s wise to moderate it

Here are some of the things I tell my clients:

--- Never take caffeine within 90 min upon waking

(this is when your body produces its'' cortisol - aka, natural energy, if you take caffeine during this time you will diminish your natural energy and crash later in the day)

--- Stop taking caffeine 10 hours pre-bedtime

(so you fall into a deeper sleep more easily)

--- Drink your coffee black

(or put cinnamon in it if you''re fasting - and protein powder if you''re in your eating window)

--- Your pre-workout shouldn''t have a ton of ingredients

(just caffeine and some amino acids, and stay away from those with words such as ''explode'', ''beast'', and ''veins'' in the title)

--- Max out your total caffeine intake to 300-400 mg per day

(combined over 2-4 servings throughout the day)

--- Put L-Theanine in your coffee or pre-workout

(this will ''prolong'' the effects of your caffeine, so you end up needing less)', false) on conflict (id) do update set title = excluded.title, video_url = coalesce(public.lessons.video_url, excluded.video_url), body = coalesce(public.lessons.body, excluded.body), retired = excluded.retired;
insert into public.lessons (id, kind, number, title, video_url, body, retired) values ('c0f12f38-f347-5567-a73f-3244b3a7b094', 'sbw', 44, 'The 3 fastest (and best) ways to properly burn fat', 'https://youtu.be/6Wc0bSfjgVk', 'If you want to lose fat once and for all, watch this video

Not only did it take me a couple days to make, but it''s one of the most thorough ones yet

It will reveal everything you need to know for everlasting results.

Not just in fat loss, but also in:

- the best types of cardio to do

- why heavy weights are better than light weights

- why cardio is overrated

- the single biggest determinant on whether you lose fat and keep it off, or yo-yo forever

No fluff, straight to the point

Watch this video', false) on conflict (id) do update set title = excluded.title, video_url = coalesce(public.lessons.video_url, excluded.video_url), body = coalesce(public.lessons.body, excluded.body), retired = excluded.retired;
insert into public.lessons (id, kind, number, title, video_url, body, retired) values ('178df414-68a6-5c5d-8e2d-ed53838d3455', 'sbw', 45, 'Do you need heavy weights or light weights to get definition?', 'https://youtu.be/MSK-6Dk6MRc', 'If someone says they want ''definition''...

What they''re saying is that they want to ''see their muscles''

And everyone has all kinds of muscles.

You as well.

Some of us have it wrapped in fat though.

Lots of it.

So to start ''seeing'' the muscles... What do you need to do?

You need to lose fat

This is where most people think they can ''burn it off''

So they start working out more

More activity

Then they check their activity monitors and see how many calories they''re ''burning''... thinking that they''re literally burning fat

But if you''ve been following me for a while now, you know you can''t burn fat through exercise

Some people are stubborn, and they still try.

But they''re all fat.

To burn fat, you need to shrink your fat cells.

And you do that with your food.

Caloric deficits, and all that stuff.

But it''s Friday, and you don''t want to hear any of that.

So, back to the lecture at hand. (Perfection is perfected so I''ma let ''em understand)

What''s the difference between heavy weights and light weights?

Does that extra work ''burn off'' the fat?

Or does it not really matter?

Or should you actually lift heavier weights?

To see the truth, the whole gosh dang truth, and nothing but - watch this video', false) on conflict (id) do update set title = excluded.title, video_url = coalesce(public.lessons.video_url, excluded.video_url), body = coalesce(public.lessons.body, excluded.body), retired = excluded.retired;
insert into public.lessons (id, kind, number, title, video_url, body, retired) values ('ea0ef443-ff86-51c6-a33a-816241e350f8', 'sbw', 46, 'Here''s why you should be jumping rope more often...', 'https://youtu.be/Hl9ZjQObtBY', 'If you''re not doing it already - jumping rope is one of the best ways of doing cardio

Average session is 10-ish minutes

You become good in just 2-3x week

Can be done anywhere

And it has a myriad of benefits

It improves your ankle mobility

Improves your ''gait''

Burns calories

But ALSO, just like with hill sprints, you can''t really get injured on it

Here''s an 80-sec video I made for you on why this is - and how to switch up your routine when you jump

If you have legs, there''s really no excuse not to do jump rope', false) on conflict (id) do update set title = excluded.title, video_url = coalesce(public.lessons.video_url, excluded.video_url), body = coalesce(public.lessons.body, excluded.body), retired = excluded.retired;
insert into public.lessons (id, kind, number, title, video_url, body, retired) values ('00593713-b86a-547a-bf95-a0616e6c70bc', 'sbw', 47, '4 tips to get more out of your caffeine intake', 'https://youtu.be/XwlHgbfBwSc', 'Caffeine in itself is not considered a ''controlled substance''

But for many Americans, it''s a daily drug that they NEED to get going

I think caffeine is very, very awesome

But as with everything - when used in moderation only

And too many people rely on it a little too much

(always perfectly visible at airports and gyms)

Here''s a quick unedited video I shot answering a question I got from a client:

"Is caffeine bad for you?"

Spoiler alert - it''s not.

But it also kinda depends.

Check this video for the full answer, along with 4 techniques to get the most out of your caffeine usage.', false) on conflict (id) do update set title = excluded.title, video_url = coalesce(public.lessons.video_url, excluded.video_url), body = coalesce(public.lessons.body, excluded.body), retired = excluded.retired;
insert into public.lessons (id, kind, number, title, video_url, body, retired) values ('1f69df15-ea1a-5cf5-9195-1546afc99c64', 'sbw', 48, 'How to get motivated again', 'https://youtu.be/EN5qOYCXKFM', 'Back in 2006 when I moved from Holland to USA, I was motivated

I was in my late twenties, committed to make it happen in this beautiful country. Do or die trying.

I remember seeing a Lamborghini Murcielago drive down Sunset Blvd, thinking to myself "this is where it''s at"

I had tunnel vision

Whatever it took, I would do it. And after being laid off as an engineer, I went all in on personal training

I did have a girlfriend at the time, but tbh - all my focus was on my career

Listening to Napoleon Hill in my car, hiring coaches, adhering to strict schedules, nothing was left to chance

Then fast forward to 7 years later, I had 3 locations - big staff, together serving over 1,000 clients every month

And as I started ''basking'' in my new reality, I started letting go of my habits

Very slowly though.

It''s not even that I got worse per se, it''s more that I stopped ''growing'' with the same intensity

Until I got stagnant, and over time many of the habits that got me to where I was were GONE

It''s the age old ''what got you there is not what will keep you there''

Combined with the fact that I thought I had ''arrived''

And slowly but surely, I started getting lazy myself

I was probably eating 4,000 calories every day, and I went from 25+ audiobooks per year to maybe 3

Once you stop exercising, things get flaccid

And once you stop ''exercising your brain'', your brain gets weak

That''s why your life should be 1 long ride of ''slight discomfort''

Comfort once in a while is nice

But it''s outside your comfort where all growth happens

And happiness comes from being productive

To be productive, you have to increase your capacity - and that comes with staying out of that comfort zone.

Here''s a video that is an excerpt of a coaching call I did last week.

An online client asked me how he can get his motivation back, because he keeps waking up lazy, not wanting to exercise.

Check the video for my response, and how I see things currently in my own life as well.', false) on conflict (id) do update set title = excluded.title, video_url = coalesce(public.lessons.video_url, excluded.video_url), body = coalesce(public.lessons.body, excluded.body), retired = excluded.retired;
insert into public.lessons (id, kind, number, title, video_url, body, retired) values ('ab86f901-2133-5d70-b70e-daf14d8a4ad6', 'sbw', 49, '4 things to know about pre-workouts', 'https://youtu.be/Vl9TbH7LBEQ', 'Here''s everything you need to know about pre-workouts

It''s not my shortest video ever made.

But you will learn:

- whether you can have coffee and pre-workout on the same day

- the 1 mistake most Americans don''t tackle before taking their pre-workout

- what happens if you ''over caffeinate'' yourself (and how to know if you''re there already)

- how I used to take pre-workouts that had DMT in them, and what they did to me

- a message to 20-year old kids that will lengthen their life and increase the quality of it', false) on conflict (id) do update set title = excluded.title, video_url = coalesce(public.lessons.video_url, excluded.video_url), body = coalesce(public.lessons.body, excluded.body), retired = excluded.retired;
insert into public.lessons (id, kind, number, title, video_url, body, retired) values ('c972b824-9f87-51bb-bb43-1e26ad18b67f', 'sbw', 50, '"Why am I not losing weight anymore?"', 'https://youtu.be/VuT0xVorX30', 'If you set out to lose weight, set goals, you start eating better, you start exercising…

And you go hard for a couple weeks...

And the scale hasn’t moved...?

THIS

... is when the average person (with no ‘reason why’) will stop (and try again next year)

This is often also where people will get back on their prescription meds (and live a downward spiraling life)

If you''re doing everything right, but not losing weight, the solution is way more simple than you think

Here''s a quick video with 3 things to go over first

In this video you''ll see 3 ''questions'' you have to ask yourself

Pass these 3 questions, and you can change your approach

But 99% of the time, these 3 questions will give you the clarity you need to keep going (and eventually hit your goal weight with ease).', false) on conflict (id) do update set title = excluded.title, video_url = coalesce(public.lessons.video_url, excluded.video_url), body = coalesce(public.lessons.body, excluded.body), retired = excluded.retired;
insert into public.lessons (id, kind, number, title, video_url, body, retired) values ('d07b6f6e-43ac-5108-b29d-87517c4c2e73', 'sbw', 51, '4 tips to make your veggies taste better', 'https://youtu.be/2Gb1FQuqLLo', 'With all due respect, but people who don''t eat vegetables NEVER look happy

You can always tell who doesn''t eat their veggies

Here are 4 ways you can see if someone if eating their vegetables

Along with 4 tips to get more vegetables in yourself (if you''re one of ''those people'')

P.S. The problem with vegetables = most people think they''re boring

But in today''s video I tell you 4 tips to make them taste amazing (really, awesome flavor guarantee)

P.P.S. If you''re too busy to watch my 4-min video I painstakingly made for you and you alone, the 4 tips are:
- Cook asparagus in garlic grass-fed butter
- Smoke some sprouts with cheese over them
- Put spinach in your protein shakes
- Grow up already', false) on conflict (id) do update set title = excluded.title, video_url = coalesce(public.lessons.video_url, excluded.video_url), body = coalesce(public.lessons.body, excluded.body), retired = excluded.retired;
insert into public.lessons (id, kind, number, title, video_url, body, retired) values ('308df9ba-d80f-54ca-b2b2-361d6ebb83d1', 'sbw', 52, '4 tips to get out of a rut', 'https://youtu.be/htLlimzIkAU', 'About 40 million Americans suffer from anxiety and depression

That''s 20% of the entire country

(1 in 5 people across all ages)

... that''s a lot

While I do believe the majority of depressions start with the mere fact of breaking promises to yourself

And no amount of pills or external help will be as paramount as your own thoughts and self-care,

... I also don''t believe you''re always at 100% of your functioning

The only people who are 100% picture-perfect all the time are in movies or on your timeline

We all climb mountains in life, and sometimes we find ourselves in ''valleys of despair''

(either due to trauma, or being in the wrong social and/or digital environment)

That being said, I do believe you can ''autoregulate'' yourself

There are 4 ''areas'' in your life that...

(if you keep a close eye on them)

... will tell you whether you''re ok - or if you''re on your way to being in a rut

I put these 4 areas in this quick video right here.

If you keep track of these 4 areas, you will avoid that rut

Because a minor rut can quickly turn into a mild depression

And ''mild'' gets ''severe'' fast if you don''t handle it

And antidepressants are always lurking

Most people consider big pharma to be ''normal''

But once you take synthetic antidepressants, your dependance on them grows, and your entire life will be one big downward spiral

Here''s a video on this topic, I hope you get something out of it - or if you know someone whom you feel is headed in the wrong direction, send it over in a tactful way

So much mental suffering can be avoided with common sense and appropriate amounts of discomfort

Especially with mental health, the whole ''ounce of prevention = pound of cure'' rings very true', false) on conflict (id) do update set title = excluded.title, video_url = coalesce(public.lessons.video_url, excluded.video_url), body = coalesce(public.lessons.body, excluded.body), retired = excluded.retired;
insert into public.lessons (id, kind, number, title, video_url, body, retired) values ('5fa60306-77ff-5deb-87db-18cd0a1a99ed', 'smf', 1, 'What do you want?', null, 'You will never achieve anything if you can not work yourself into a white heat of desire and actually believe that you will achieve what you want.

This is why you need what''s called ''definiteness of purpose''

Or in other words, you need to know:
- exactly what you want in life
- and the reason why you want it.

It sounds simple, and it is.

(here''s a little secret btw - almost all success in life is very simple)

But ''simple'' does not mean easy.

And what''s ''simple'' to do... is easy to ignore.

So now you''re in my coaching program, get off to a strong start and do this...

Follow these 6 steps for you to set yourself up for success:

1.Set in your mind the exact results you desire. Be DEFINITE.

2.Determine exactly what you will give to get those results (there is no such thing as something for nothing).

3.Establish a definite date when you intend to get these results.

4.Write it all out. Everything from points 1-3 in a short summary.

5. Read that summary out, twice daily. Once in the morning, once in the afternoon. See, feel, and believe yourself already having these results.

6.Create a plan for carrying it all out

And lastly, begin at once, even if you''re not ready.

That means right now.

Your thoughts are way more powerful than you think.

Your thoughts will be the main difference between successfully losing weight, or yo-yo-ing till you die.

Get your thoughts under control asap, and you will be able to accomplish anything you want.

Click here to check in for your first week:
{Training Magic Link training_slug=week-2-habits-and-homework}

Once you complete your check-in, you''ll be given instructions on what to do in week 2.', false) on conflict (id) do update set title = excluded.title, video_url = coalesce(public.lessons.video_url, excluded.video_url), body = coalesce(public.lessons.body, excluded.body), retired = excluded.retired;
insert into public.lessons (id, kind, number, title, video_url, body, retired) values ('ac3096e8-7f76-5cfc-89c6-9873056e7bc3', 'smf', 2, 'Luck doesn''t exist', null, '"When faith is mixed with thought, your subconscious mind will translate it into its spiritual equivalent, which is infinite intelligence" - Napoleon Hill

The above quote sums up how nobody is every doomed to bad luck

In fact, from now on I want you to live in a world where luck does not even exist

Here''s how this works:

You know how a submarine has a periscope?

The entire submarine is under water, and ONE person can look through the periscope

That ONE person will have the power to tell everyone aboard the submarine what''s happening above sea level

Whatever orders that ONE person gives, the entire submarine will follow instantly

All the crew aboard blindly trust this ONE person

This ONE person is you and your conscious thinking

And the entire submarine is your subconscious mind

Whatever you decide to think, your subconscious will act on

Whether it''s positive or negative...

Your subconscious mind will move on whatever thoughts you feed it

So...

You want to get lucky?

You want the number on the scale to go down?

Your business to thrive?

Relationships to flourish?

Then feed yourself positive thoughts

It''s the only way you will voluntarily develop good faith (aka, a strong subconscious mind),

Nobody is doomed to bad luck

Because whatever is picked up by your subconscious mind will be translated into its physical equivalent.

Now you''re probably thinking: "where do I start with this?", "what thoughts should I think then?"

Start with these 5...

Repeat these daily to become self-reliant, successful, and finally lose some serious weight and keep it off:

1. I know I have the ability to get in shape. Therefore I demand from myself persistent continuous action and I promise to do just that.

2. I realize that thoughts become things. Therefore I will concentrate daily on who I want to become and exactly who/what I want to have in my life.

3. I have clearly written down my goals and I will never stop trying until I have developed sufficient self-confidence for their attainment.

4. I will concentrate on my desire until it becomes a burning obsession. And I will do this by reading my goals out loud daily and back them with emotion.

5. I understand that I become who I surround myself with. Therefore I will succeed by attracting to myself the forces which I choose to use and the cooperation of other people. I will eliminate hatred, envy, jealousy, selfishness and cynicism by developing love for all. Because I know that a negative attitude towards others can never bring me success. I will cause others to believe in me because I believe in them (and in myself).

Remember - luck doesn''t exist

Luck is merely a word used by those who don''t understand the power of their very own thoughts.

Everything you want is right within your grasp.

Your submarine crew is ready and eagerly waiting for your instructions - what are you going to tell them?

Click here to check in for Week 2:
{Training Magic Link training_slug=week-3-habits-and-homework}

Once you complete your check-in, you''ll be given instructions on what to do in week 3.

Michael', false) on conflict (id) do update set title = excluded.title, video_url = coalesce(public.lessons.video_url, excluded.video_url), body = coalesce(public.lessons.body, excluded.body), retired = excluded.retired;
insert into public.lessons (id, kind, number, title, video_url, body, retired) values ('1484a1ad-fd00-5baa-af92-c9b8b2f930c2', 'smf', 3, 'Dealing with setbacks', null, 'As you set out to lose weight, you will encounter setbacks

We all go through this

Some weeks you''ll do everything perfect and the scale won''t move

Other weeks you''ll completely fall of the wagon and mess up on your food

When this happens, it''s important not to react - but instead, to respond.

And the difference is in how you respond...

Especially when things get tough. You might start thinking like a failure...

Like you were never meant to succeed anyway.

But, remember -> Every failure brings with it the seed of an equivalent success.

When your plans fail, it does not mean failure.

It means you need to build stronger plans.

Because a quitter never wins, and a winner never quits.

Whenever you face adversity, prove to yourself that your philosophy can take care of the situation of failure.

For defeat is never failure. No circumstance is ever failure until it is accepted by the individual as such.

You can always profit through adversity, by staying at it.

Where everyone else would give up, you reinvent yourself and you keep going.

That''s how winning is done.

Click here to check in for Week 3:
{Training Magic Link training_slug=week-4-habits-and-homework}

Once you complete your check-in you will see your Week 4 Habits & Homework.', false) on conflict (id) do update set title = excluded.title, video_url = coalesce(public.lessons.video_url, excluded.video_url), body = coalesce(public.lessons.body, excluded.body), retired = excluded.retired;
insert into public.lessons (id, kind, number, title, video_url, body, retired) values ('eae52de6-4e37-5ad1-9794-3bfbc5b189cc', 'smf', 4, 'Going the Extra Mile', null, 'There is one major requirement for successfully losing weight that you will never hear in popular media or advertisements

Even those who lost weight and kept it off will not tell you, because for them it probably comes natural

This one requirement is going the extra mile

Going the extra mile is when you''re doing more than what is asked, doing more than what is asked all the time, and doing more than what is asked, all the time, with a pleasant attitude.

And it is the ONLY way you can make life pay you whatever you want

But it''s never talked about

Because it''s hard to do, and even harder to sell

But have you ever seen someone do good at first...

Then next year they do better?

And years later you find out they''ve been doing better every single year, constantly improving?

It''s because they kept going the extra mile, and in doing so they increased the returns that gave them above-average results

In other words, the longer you go the extra mile - the bigger your returns get

Like magic, it compounds over time

Going the extra mile for a couple days does nothing.

Doing it for months, years - will change your life. Add to the fact that you will start getting ‘lucky breaks’.

And... your ‘doing extra’ with a pleasing attitude will improve your personality and improve your imagination.

This is because you’re constantly seeking new and better ways to do things.

Lastly, going the extra mile kills procrastination (which is the #1 cause of failure)

In case you''re not convinced just yet, here are 5 benefits of going the extra mile:

1. You stand out from most - for most don''t even go the first mile. It shows your trainer/coach that you''re in this to win it. And your trainer/coach will probably take you very serious.

2. It leads to a mental growth and physical perfection throughout all aspects of your life.

3. It protects you against adversity. Because it develops self reliance.

4. It leads to the development of a positive and pleasing personal attitude.

5. It is the only justifiable reason to ask for favors from others.

Don''t be like everyone else - complaining that things are hard

Take on the work, and do more than what''s expected of you

Within no time you''ll be miles further than you''ve ever been in your life.

Click here to check in for Week 4:
{Training Magic Link training_slug=week-5-habits-and-homework}

Once you complete your check-in, you will be given your instructions on what to do in Week 5.', false) on conflict (id) do update set title = excluded.title, video_url = coalesce(public.lessons.video_url, excluded.video_url), body = coalesce(public.lessons.body, excluded.body), retired = excluded.retired;
insert into public.lessons (id, kind, number, title, video_url, body, retired) values ('40600ac1-ac3d-5b9c-b621-7795beb29a97', 'smf', 5, 'Fear & Doubt', null, 'As mentioned in your earlier STRONG MIND emails, you and I have 100% control over just 1 thing in our life...

Our own mindset.

We all know it

But most people don’t realize the power this gives us - as most people still live in fear and doubt

When you live in fear and doubt, it simply means you dwell on the things you do NOT want in your life

How do you fix this?

Simple, you use applied faith, take possession of your mind, and think of the things you DO want in life.

You will always attract what you think and believe.

So choose wisely.

The one thing that separates successful people from those who live in fear and doubt is that the successful have a capacity for belief

Failures see the hole in the donut

Successful people see the donut around the hole

Success requires belief, and the first ''thing'' to believe in is yourself.

Here are 5 steps to strengthen your applied faith:

-1- Know what you want and believe you will get it

-2- Express gratitude many times, every day for that which you want - even BEFORE you actually get it. All possession starts in the mind.

-3- Be ready to act immediately on ''gut feelings''

-4- When overtaken by defeat, remember that your faith will be tested many times before you get what you want

-5- Possess a burning desire for what you want

With 100% control over what you put in your mind, you can literally attract whichever you demand in life.

Remember, faith is something you already have. However if you’re like most people, you’re using it wrong by focusing on what you do not want.

Direct all your thoughts towards what you want

You''ll be amazed by how your life will change

Click here to check in for Week 5:
{Training Magic Link training_slug=week-6-habits-and-homework}

