insert into public.lessons (id, kind, number, title, video_url, body, retired) values ('c728808c-699e-5632-a4c5-91ac4dc8ff9e', 'smf', 20, 'Don''t let perfect get in the way of possible', null, 'If you want to know one of my greatest weaknesses, it''s wanting everything to be JUST PERFECT

(and anything less than perfection sucks)

I''ve gotten better

But just last month my business coach told me to stop ''perpetually preparing''

He said:

"When you try to turn the wheels of a car, what''s easier?..."

"When the car is standing still?"

"Or when the car is moving?"

Obviously, the answer is when the cat is moving

And it doesn''t even have to be going fast

But ''changing direction'' is so much easier when you''re also executing

And executing... is essential for success

You can have the greatest meal plan (like, the one you got from me)

But if you don''t read & eat it, you''ll get chubby

With that said though...

The ONLY way you will consistently execute is when your plan is actually possible

And what''s possible for one is impossible for the other

There is no shame in this

Some have more time and money than others

You have to find what''s good for you

Look at your commitment...

Your resources...

Your available time

... and then ''start where you are''

Keep moving forward, no matter how slow you might go

Imperfect action always beats standing still

Click here to check in for Week 20:
{Training Magic Link training_slug=week-21-habits-and-homework}

