insert into public.lessons (id, kind, number, title, video_url, body, retired) values ('59fa4e01-709a-57af-a754-d45140a291e9', 'smf', 21, 'Help others win', null, 'Ever had it where someone else is getting way better results, and they''re doing the ex-act same thing you are?

And perhaps this made you feel a little envious (or a little jealous)?

It happens to the best of us.

And it gives us a short-term dopamine hit, to somehow ''downplay'' other peoples successes.

But overall, life is always better when you applaud when others win

Even if you''re struggling at the moment. And someone else is taking off.

When you get excited for other people''s victories, you open yourself up to learn from them.

Even more, you attract their energy into your own life

(so in the end, it only helps all parties involved)

Doing so, you will be way more likely to win bigger yourself

Then when YOU win, you can be there for others when they’re down.

But it all starts with becoming that person who claps for others.

It might be a character change, but it''s worth it.

Click here to check in for Week 21:
{Training Magic Link training_slug=week-22-habits-and-homework}

