insert into public.lessons (id, kind, number, title, video_url, body, retired) values ('77d8904e-2483-5ffc-9e0d-a9be9d8cf5f1', 'smf', 25, 'If you still mess up bad on food, it''s because of this...', null, 'It''s not because healthy food tastes bad

(because it doesn''t - Himalayan Sea Salt or cinnamon can fix anything)

It''s not because you just HAVE to eat those donuts

(because you don''t - you''re a grown-up)

Whether you''re going it alone, have a gym membership, or you have a coach

The #1 reason you''re not following your meal plan is because your desire is too weak

Weak desires produce weak results, like small fires produce small amounts of heat.

If this is you, my advice is to go back to the drawing board....

1. First off... know what you want

2. Secondly... realize why you want it, and work yourself into a white heat of desire

3. Then... believe in your ability to follow through in getting what you want.

Make your plan to get what you want ''definite'' and ''doable''

Meaning, organize your plans. However weak your plans may be, you''re more likely to show persistence if they''re organized.

And make them doable for your current skills and capabilities.

As you ''restart'' your journey, you will automatically build new habits.

And with all that... results will come.

And with RESULTS, everything changes. This is when you will no longer ''not follow'' your meal plan.

It''s that initial ''pain period'' of no results that you have to break through first.

That''s the hardest part.

After that, it''s all smooth sailing.

Click here to check in for Week 25:
{Training Magic Link training_slug=week-26-habits-and-homework}

