insert into public.lessons (id, kind, number, title, video_url, body, retired) values ('71ad143e-6431-5bd8-b65d-ee870c69f27b', 'smf', 27, 'Your 6 biggest fears (and how to fight them)', null, 'Thoughts from others will affect your destiny just as hard as your very own thoughts

That''s why in this email I want to remind you...

That YOU have the capability to select your thoughts, and which thoughts you receive from others.

You already know by now, everything in the world starts out as a thought.

This is why thoughts of ''fear'' will never translate into courageous things.

The 6 basic fears we all must fight every day are:

1. Death
2. Poverty
3. Criticism
4. Old Age
5. Bad Health
6. Loss of loved ones

All of the above are legit fears, and nobody will blame you for ''worrying'' about them

(this is what the news does every single day)

My advice though, if you want a rich life - is to eliminate worry all together.

Here''s how:

Fear of death -> Decide to accept death as an inescapable event.

Fear of poverty -> Decide to get along with whatever wealth you will accumulate without worrying.

Fear of criticism -> Decide to not worry about what others think or say.

Fear of old age -> Decide to accept it as a blessing which brings great wisdom, self-control, and understanding not known to youth.

Fear of Bad Health -> Decide to eat the meal plan your trainer gave you (food is your medicine)

Fear of loss of loved one -> Decide to get along without love if necessary.

Nothing that life has to offer is worth the price of worry.

Coming to this decision will bring you poise, peace of mind, and calmness of thought.

And this will bring happiness.

When you''re full of fear, you not only destroy your own chances of intelligent action, but you also transmit these vibrations to the minds of anyone you come into contact with, and thus you destroy their chances as well.

Kill the fear

Click here to check in for Week 27:
{Training Magic Link training_slug=week-28-habits-and-homework}

Once you complete your check-in, you''ll be given instructions on what to do in week 28.', false) on conflict (id) do update set title = excluded.title, video_url = coalesce(public.lessons.video_url, excluded.video_url), body = coalesce(public.lessons.body, excluded.body), retired = excluded.retired;
insert into public.lessons (id, kind, number, title, video_url, body, retired) values ('eb91964b-49f1-5e8a-9d0b-cb800dab1273', 'smf', 28, 'The key to a beautiful life', null, 'Today''s email is inspired by the very last paragraph of ''Think and Grow Rich''

The whole book is one of my favorites. It''s one of those books where every line is gold.

But that last paragraph... it wakes you up:

"Life is a checkerboard, and the player opposite you is time. If you hesitate before moving, or neglect a move promptly, your men will be wiped off the board by time. You are playing against a partner who will not tolerate indecision. Learning to control your thoughts puts you in possession of the master key that unlocks the door to life’s bountiful riches. You can force life to pay whatever is asked. The master key is the privilege of creating in your own mind a burning desire for a definite form of riches. There is only a price to pay if you do not use it, and that price is failure."

You''ll have to read that a couple times to absorb it all

And perhaps you''ll have to revisit it when you feel the need

But if there''s just one thing you get from the above

It''s that using the ability to control your thoughts will give you a beautiful life

And the keyword here being ''using''

You already have this ability

You can start using it, right now

When you do, life will pay you back tenfold

If you don''t, your life will end in failure

Control your thoughts

Click here to check in for Week 28:
{Training Magic Link training_slug=week-29-habits-and-homework}

