insert into public.lessons (id, kind, number, title, video_url, body, retired) values ('d0a6005c-85d9-595a-b977-280f4dedb149', 'smf', 30, 'Act different, attract different', null, 'Your past might have been troublesome

After training people for over a decade, I''ve heard all kinds of stories

People who have been ridiculed by others, violated, cheated, lost everything, divorced, lost loved ones, disease, etc.

We all have ''something'' that has happened to us

And that ''something'' can weigh us down for the rest of our lives

But those ''somethings'' aren''t who you are

Who you are is who you have decided to be

... by the actions you have taken so far

As long as you don''t blame your circumstances, none of your past challenges can define you,

See most people move like this: They feel something (angry, hurt, disappointed, etc)... so they do something about it... and that creates their identity

A better way is to turn this around

DECIDE who you want to be first. Choose your identity, regardless of how you feel at the time.

Then take action in line with your new identity

And this will make you feel the way you want

Now ask yourself, who do you want to become?

Then act as if you''re already that exact person

It''s uneasy at first, but it''s a surefire way to accelerate yourself into your ideal self

Click here to check in for Week 30:
{Training Magic Link training_slug=week-31-habits-and-homework}

